fect areas. Finally, the detected defects were categorized according to their morphology. Experimental results show that the proposed method using 3D laser scanning data can detect and classify typical welding defects with an accuracy of more than 97.1%. Furthermore, different types of defects, including holes, undercuts, and craters, can also be accurately detected with precision 98.9%.", "作者": ["Hanjie Huang", "Bin Zhou", "Songxiao Cao", "Tao Song", "Zhipeng Xu", "Qing Jiang"], "年份": 2025, "发表位置": "Sensors"}}'}], 'model': 'DeepSeek-V4-Flash[free]', 'max_tokens': 4000, 'reasoning_effort': 'none', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0}} | ctx={"client_host": "127.0.0.1", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/sessions/b28569c2810d4c95a568626d927b3740/runs", "run_id": "run_abc3fcaca9164d70ac2d7c7d70a2f67e", "session_key": "b28569c2810d4c95a568626d927b3740", "turn_id": "834e741a-5514-4b36-8a6c-8f05e80a1c81"}
