ified Crack and Surface Defect Dataset for Robust Structural Damage Detection",\n              "authors": [\n                "Misbah Ijaz",\n                "Saif Ur Rehman Khan",\n                "Abd Ur Rehman",\n                "Sebastian Vollmer",\n                "Andreas Dengel",\n                "Muhammad Nabeel Asim"\n              ],\n              "year": 2026,\n              "abstract": "Automated detection and classification of structural cracks and surface defects is a critical challenge in civil engineering, infrastructure maintenance, and heritage preservation. Recent advances in Computer Vision (CV) and Deep Learning (DL) have significantly improved automatic crack detection. However, these methods rely heavily on large, diverse, and carefully curated datasets that include various crack types across different surface materials. Many existing public crack datasets lack geographic diversity, surface types, scale, and labeling consistency, making it challenging for trained algorithms to generalize effectively in real world conditions. We provide a novel dataset, StructDamage, a curated collection of approximately 78,093 images spanning nine surface types: walls, tile, stone, road, pavement, deck, concrete, and brick. The dataset was constructed by systematically aggregating, harmonizing, and reannotating images from 32 publicly available datasets covering concrete structures, asphalt pavements, masonry walls, bridges, and historic buildings. All images are organized in a folder level classification hierarchy suitable for training Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and Vision Transformers. To highlight the practical value of the dataset, we present baseline classification results using fifteen DL architectures from six model families, with twelve achieving macro F1-scores over 0.96. The best performing model DenseNet201 achieves 98.62% accuracy. The proposed dataset provides a comprehensive and versatile resource suitable for classification tasks. With thorough documentation and a standard structure, it is designed to promote reproducible research and support the development and fair evaluation of robust crack damage detection approaches.",\n              "source": "arxiv",\n              "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.10484v1",\n              "publication_date": "2026-03-11T07:17:19Z",\n              "journal/conference": "arXiv",\n              "journal_conference": "arXiv",\n              "volume": "",\n              "issue": "",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "arXiv",\n              "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.10484v1",\n              "doi": null,\n              "metadata": {\n                "published": "2026-03-11T07:17:19Z",\n                "arxiv_id": "2603.10484v1",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "arxiv"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "如何构建一个大规模、多样化且标注一致的港口集装箱损伤检测数据集，以提升结构损伤检测算法的泛化能力？",\n              "methods": [\n                "系统性地聚合、协调和重新标注来自32个公开数据集的图像",\n                "构建包含约78,093张图像、涵盖9种表面类型的数据集StructDamage",\n                "采用文件夹级别的分类层次结构，适用于CNN和Vision Transformer训练",\n                "使用15种深度学习架构（来自6个模型家族）进行基线分类实验"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "StructDamage数据集",\n                "32个公开数据集（涵盖混凝土结构、沥青路面、砖石墙、桥梁和历史建筑）"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "提供了StructDamage数据集，包含约78,093张图像和9种表面类型",\n                "通过系统聚合和重新标注解决了现有数据集地理多样性、表面类型、规模和标注一致性的不足",\n                "提供了15种深度学习架构的基线分类结果，其中12种宏F1分数超过0.96",\n                "最佳模型DenseNet201达到98.62%的准确率"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [\n                "论文未明确提及港口集装箱损伤检测的具体应用场景或数据",\n                "数据集主要针对结构裂缝和表面缺陷，未专门针对港口集装箱损伤进行优化"\n              ],\n              "main_results": [\n                "12种深度学习架构的宏F1分数超过0.96",\n                "最佳模型DenseNet201达到98.62%的准确率"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "论文提出了StructDamage数据集，通过聚合和重新标注32个公开数据集，构建了包含约78,093张图像、9种表面类型的大规模结构损伤检测数据集，并展示了15种深度学习架构的基线分类结果，其中DenseNet201达到98.62%的准确率。",\n              "missing_information": [\n                "论文未提及港口集装箱损伤检测的具体数据或实验",\n                "未说明数据集在港口集装箱场景下的适用性或验证结果"\n              ],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        },\n        {\n          "paperId": "2501.16662v2",\n          "status": "ok",\n          "extraction": {\n            "paper": {\n              "id": "2501.16662v2",\n              "paperId": "2501.16662v2",\n              "title": "Vision-based autonomous structural damage detection using data-driven methods",\n              "authors": [\n                "Seyyed Taghi Ataei",\n                "Parviz Mohammad Zadeh",\n                "Saeid Ataei"\n              ],\n              "year": 2025,\n              "abstract": "This study addresses the urgent need for efficient and accurate damage detection in wind turbine structures, a crucial component of renewable energy infrastructure. Traditional inspection methods, such as manual assessments and non-destructive testing (NDT), are often costly, time-consuming, and prone to human error. To tackle these challenges, this research investigates advanced deep learning algorithms for vision-based structural health monitoring (SHM). A dataset of wind turbine surface images, featuring various damage types and pollution, was prepared and augmented for enhanced model training. Three algorithms-YOLOv7, its lightweight variant, and Faster R-CNN- were employed to detect and classify surface damage. The models were trained and evaluated on a dataset split into training, testing, and evaluation subsets (80%-10%-10%). Results indicate that YOLOv7 outperformed the others, achieving 82.4% mAP@50 and high processing speed, making it suitable for real-time inspections. By optimizing hyperparameters like learning rate and batch size, the models\' accuracy and efficiency improved further. YOLOv7 demonstrated significant advancements in detection precision and execution speed, especially for real-time applications. However, challenges such as dataset limitations and environmental variability were noted, suggesting future work on segmentation methods and larger datasets. This research underscores the potential of vision-based deep learning techniques to transform SHM practices by reducing costs, enhancing safety, and improving reliability, thus contributing to the sustainable maintenance of critical infrastructure and supporting the longevity of wind energy systems.",\n              "source": "arxiv",\n              "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2501.16662v2",\n              "publication_date": "2025-01-28T02:52:04Z",\n              "journal/conference": "arXiv",\n              "journal_conference": "arXiv",\n              "volume": "",\n              "issue": "",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "arXiv",\n              "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.16662v2",\n              "doi": null,\n              "metadata": {\n                "published": "2025-01-28T02:52:04Z",\n                "arxiv_id": "2501.16662v2",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "基于视觉的集装箱损伤检测",\n                    "keyword": "(container damage detection and computer vision) or (container surface defect and deep learning)"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱损伤的自动检测系统",\n                    "keyword": "(automated inspection and container damage) or (port container and defect detection system)"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "arxiv"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "如何利用基于视觉的深度学习方法实现风力涡轮机结构的自主损伤检测？",\n              "methods": [\n                "YOLOv7",\n                "YOLOv7轻量级变体",\n                "Faster R-CNN",\n                "数据增强",\n                "超参数优化（学习率、批量大小）"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "风力涡轮机表面图像数据集（包含多种损伤类型和污染）"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "研究了YOLOv7、其轻量级变体和Faster R-CNN三种算法在风力涡轮机表面损伤检测中的应用",\n                "通过超参数优化提升了模型的准确性和效率",\n                "展示了YOLOv7在实时检测中的优越性能（82.4% mAP@50和高处理速度）"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [\n                "数据集有限",\n                "环境变异性影响检测效果"\n              ],\n              "main_results": [\n                "YOLOv7在检测精度和执行速度上优于其他模型，适用于实时检测",\n                "YOLOv7达到82.4% mAP@50"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "该研究针对风力涡轮机结构损伤检测的需求，采用YOLOv7、其轻量级变体和Faster R-CNN三种深度学习算法，基于增强后的表面图像数据集进行训练和评估。结果表明YOLOv7在精度和速度上表现最佳，适合实时检测，但存在数据集和环境变异性等局限。",\n              "missing_information": [],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        },\n        {\n          "paperId": "10.3390/jimaging9100193",\n          "status": "ok",\n          "extraction": {\n            "paper": {\n              "id": "10.3390/jimaging9100193",\n              "paperId": "10.3390/jimaging9100193",\n              "title": "A Systematic Review on Deep Learning with CNNs Applied to Surface Defect Detection",\n              "authors": [\n                "Esteban Cumbajin",\n                "Nuno Rodrigues",\n                "Paulo Manuel Costa",\n                "Rolando Miragaia",\n                "Luís Frazão",\n                "Nuno Costa",\n                "Antonio Fernández‐Caballero",\n                "Jorge Carneiro",\n                "L.H. Buruberri",\n                "Ántónio Pereira"\n              ],\n              "year": 2023,\n              "abstract": "Surface defect detection with machine learning has become an important tool in industries and a large field of study for researchers or workers in recent years. It is necessary to have a simplified source of information that helps us to better focus on one type of surface. In this systematic review, we present a classification for surface defect detection based on convolutional neural networks (CNNs) focused on surface types. Findings: Out of 253 records identified, 59 primary studies were eligible. Following the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses (PRISMA) guidelines, we analyzed the structures of each study and the concepts related to defects and their types on surfaces. The presented review is mainly focused on finding a classification for the types of surfaces most used in industry (metal, building, ceramic, wood, and special). We delve into the specifics of each surface category, offering illustrative examples of their applications within both industrial and laboratory settings. Furthermore, we propose a new taxonomy of machine learning based on the obtained results and collected information. We summarized the studies and extracted the main characteristics such as type of surface, problem types, timeline, type of network, techniques, and datasets. Among the most relevant results of our analysis, we found that the metallic surface is the most used, as it is the one found in 62.71% of the studies, and the most prevalent problem type is classification, accounting for 49.15% of the total. Furthermore, we observe that transfer learning was employed in 83.05% of the studies, while data augmentation was utilized in 59.32%. Our findings also provide insights into the cameras most frequently employed, along with the strategies adopted to address illumination challenges present in certain articles and the approach to creating datasets for real-world applications. The main results presented in this review allow for a quick and efficient search of information for researchers and professionals interested in improving the results of their defect detection projects. Finally, we analyzed the trends that could open new fields of study for future research in the area of surface defect detection.",\n              "source": "openalex",\n              "url": "https://openalex.org/W4387052345",\n              "publication_date": "2023-09-25",\n              "journal/conference": "Journal of Imaging",\n              "journal_conference": "Journal of Imaging",\n              "volume": "9",\n              "issue": "10",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "Journal of Imaging",\n              "pdf_url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2313-433X/9/10/193/pdf?version=1695689348",\n              "doi": "10.3390/jimaging9100193",\n              "metadata": {\n                "cited_by_count": 77,\n                "type": "review",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "基于视觉的集装箱损伤检测",\n                    "keyword": "(container damage detection and computer vision) or (container surface defect and deep learning)"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "openalex"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "如何基于卷积神经网络对表面缺陷检测进行系统分类，并分析不同表面类型（金属、建筑、陶瓷、木材、特殊）的检测方法、技术趋势和数据集特征？",\n              "methods": [\n                "系统综述遵循PRISMA指南",\n                "对59篇主要研究进行结构分析",\n                "提出基于机器学习的新分类法",\n                "分析表面类型、问题类型、时间线、网络类型、技术、数据集等特征"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "未明确列出具体数据集名称，但提及了数据集创建方法用于真实世界应用"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "提出了基于表面类型的表面缺陷检测分类法",\n                "总结了金属、建筑、陶瓷、木材、特殊表面的应用实例",\n                "提供了快速高效的信息检索来源",\n                "分析了未来研究趋势"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [\n                "未明确列出局限性"\n              ],\n              "main_results": [\n                "金属表面是最常用的表面类型，占62.71%的研究",\n                "分类是最普遍的问题类型，占49.15%",\n                "迁移学习在83.05%的研究中使用",\n                "数据增强在59.32%的研究中使用",\n                "提供了常用相机和照明挑战应对策略"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "本文是一篇系统综述，基于PRISMA指南对59篇关于卷积神经网络应用于表面缺陷检测的研究进行分析，提出了基于表面类型（金属、建筑、陶瓷、木材、特殊）的分类法，总结了各表面的应用实例、技术趋势和数据集特征，发现金属表面和分类问题最为常见，迁移学习和数据增强被广泛使用。",\n              "missing_information": [\n                "未提及具体数据集名称",\n                "未明确列出局限性",\n                "未提及港口集装箱损伤检测的具体内容"\n              ],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        },\n        {\n          "paperId": "2510.21063v1",\n          "status": "ok",\n          "extraction": {\n            "paper": {\n              "id": "2510.21063v1",\n              "paperId": "2510.21063v1",\n              "title": "Deep learning-based automated damage detection in concrete structures using images from earthquake events",\n              "authors": [\n                "Abdullah Turer",\n                "Yongsheng Bai",\n                "Halil Sezen",\n                "Alper Yilmaz"\n              ],\n              "year": 2025,\n              "abstract": "Timely assessment of integrity of structures after seismic events is crucial for public safety and emergency response. This study focuses on assessing the structural damage conditions using deep learning methods to detect exposed steel reinforcement in concrete buildings and bridges after large earthquakes. Steel bars are typically exposed after concrete spalling or large flexural or shear cracks. The amount and distribution of exposed steel reinforcement is an indication of structural damage and degradation. To automatically detect exposed steel bars, new datasets of images collected after the 2023 Turkey Earthquakes were labeled to represent a wide variety of damaged concrete structures. The proposed method builds upon a deep learning framework, enhanced with fine-tuning, data augmentation, and testing on public datasets. An automated classification framework is developed that can be used to identify inside/outside buildings and structural components. Then, a YOLOv11 (You Only Look Once) model is trained to detect cracking and spalling damage and exposed bars. Another YOLO model is finetuned to distinguish different categories of structural damage levels. All these trained models are used to create a hybrid framework to automatically and reliably determine the damage levels from input images. This research demonstrates that rapid and automated damage detection following disasters is achievable across diverse damage contexts by utilizing image data collection, annotation, and deep learning approaches.",\n              "source": "arxiv",\n              "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.21063v1",\n              "publication_date": "2025-10-24T00:35:14Z",\n              "journal/conference": "arXiv",\n              "journal_conference": "arXiv",\n              "volume": "",\n              "issue": "",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "arXiv",\n              "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.21063v1",\n              "doi": null,\n              "metadata": {\n                "published": "2025-10-24T00:35:14Z",\n                "arxiv_id": "2510.21063v1",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "arxiv"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "如何利用深度学习方法从地震事件后的图像中自动检测混凝土结构的损伤（特别是暴露钢筋）？",\n              "methods": [\n                "基于深度学习的自动化分类框架，用于识别建筑内外和结构构件",\n                "YOLOv11模型训练用于检测裂缝、剥落损伤和暴露钢筋",\n                "微调另一个YOLO模型以区分不同类别的结构损伤等级",\n                "混合框架整合多个训练模型以自动可靠地确定损伤等级",\n                "数据增强和微调技术"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "2023年土耳其地震后收集的新图像数据集",\n                "公开数据集"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "提出了一个自动检测暴露钢筋的深度学习框架",\n                "创建了标注的2023年土耳其地震后混凝土结构损伤图像数据集",\n                "开发了混合框架以自动确定损伤等级"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [],\n              "main_results": [\n                "研究表明，利用图像数据收集、标注和深度学习方法，可以在不同损伤背景下实现灾后快速自动损伤检测"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "该研究聚焦于利用深度学习方法从地震事件后的图像中自动检测混凝土结构的损伤，特别是暴露钢筋。通过构建新数据集、微调YOLOv11模型并开发混合框架，实现了对裂缝、剥落和暴露钢筋的检测以及损伤等级的自动分类。",\n              "missing_information": [\n                "未提供具体的检测精度、召回率等量化性能指标",\n                "未说明数据集的具体规模（如图像数量、标注类别分布）",\n                "未提及与其他方法的对比实验结果"\n              ],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        },\n        {\n          "paperId": "s00158-025-04162-0",\n          "status": "ok",\n          "extraction": {\n            "paper": {\n              "id": "s00158-025-04162-0",\n              "paperId": "s00158-025-04162-0",\n              "title": "A generative adversarial network optimization method for damage detection and digital twinning by deep AI fault learning: Z24 Bridge structural health monitoring benchmark validation",\n              "authors": [\n                "Marios Impraimakis",\n                "Evangelia Nektaria Palkanoglou"\n              ],\n              "year": 2025,\n              "abstract": "The optimization-based damage detection and damage state digital twinning capabilities are examined here of a novel conditional-labeled generative adversarial network methodology. The framework outperforms current approaches for fault anomaly detection as no prior information is required for the health state of the system: a topic of high significance for real-world applications. Specifically, current artificial intelligence-based digital twinning approaches suffer from the uncertainty related to obtaining poor predictions when a low number of measurements is available, physics knowledge is missing, or when the damage state is unknown. To this end, an unsupervised framework is examined and validated rigorously on the benchmark structural health monitoring measurements of Z24 Bridge: a post-tensioned concrete highway bridge in Switzerland. In implementing the approach, firstly, different same damage-level measurements are used as inputs, while the model is forced to converge conditionally to two different damage states. Secondly, the process is repeated for a different group of measurements. Finally, the convergence scores are compared to identify which one belongs to a different damage state. The process for both healthy-to-healthy and damage-to-healthy input data creates, simultaneously, measurements for digital twinning purposes at different damage states, capable of pattern recognition and machine learning data generation. Further to this process, a support vector machine classifier and a principal component analysis procedure is developed to assess the generated and real measurements of each damage category, serving as a secondary new dynamics learning indicator in damage scenarios. Importantly, the approach is shown to capture accurately damage over healthy measurements, providing a powerful tool for vibration-based system-level monitoring and scalable infrastructure resilience.",\n              "source": "arxiv",\n              "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.00099v1",\n              "publication_date": "2025-10-30T16:04:47Z",\n              "journal/conference": "arXiv",\n              "journal_conference": "arXiv",\n              "volume": "",\n              "issue": "",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "arXiv",\n              "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.00099v1",\n              "doi": "s00158-025-04162-0",\n              "metadata": {\n                "published": "2025-10-30T16:04:47Z",\n                "arxiv_id": "2511.00099v1",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "arxiv"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "如何利用生成对抗网络优化方法实现无先验信息的结构损伤检测与数字孪生？",\n              "methods": [\n                "条件标记生成对抗网络（conditional-labeled GAN）",\n                "无监督学习框架",\n                "支持向量机分类器",\n                "主成分分析"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "Z24 Bridge结构健康监测基准数据"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "提出了一种无需系统健康状态先验信息的损伤检测方法",\n                "实现了不同损伤状态下的数字孪生测量生成",\n                "通过SVM和PCA提供了二次动力学学习指标"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [\n                "论文未明确说明局限性"\n              ],\n              "main_results": [\n                "该方法能够准确区分损伤与健康测量",\n                "为基于振动的系统级监测和可扩展基础设施韧性提供了有力工具"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "该论文提出了一种基于条件标记生成对抗网络的无监督优化方法，用于结构损伤检测和数字孪生，在Z24桥梁基准数据上验证了其有效性，无需先验健康状态信息。",\n              "missing_information": [\n                "未提供具体的量化性能指标（如准确率、召回率等）",\n                "未讨论方法的计算复杂度或实时性"\n              ],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        },\n        {\n          "paperId": "2506.22517v1",\n          "status": "ok",\n          "extraction": {\n            "paper": {\n              "id": "2506.22517v1",\n              "paperId": "2506.22517v1",\n              "title": "Container damage detection using advanced computer vision model Yolov12 vs Yolov11 vs RF-DETR A comparative analysis",\n              "authors": [\n                "Subhadip Kumar"\n              ],\n              "year": 2025,\n              "abstract": "Containers are an integral part of the logistics industry and act as a barrier for cargo. A typical service life for a container is more than 20 years. However, overtime containers suffer various types of damage due to the mechanical as well as natural factors. A damaged container is a safety hazard for the employees handling it and a liability for the logistic company. Therefore, a timely inspection and detection of the damaged container is a key for prolonging service life as well as avoiding safety hazards. In this paper, we will compare the performance of the damage detection by three state-of-the-art advanced computer vision models Yolov12, Yolov11 and RF-DETR. We will use a dataset of 278 annotated images to train, validate and test the model. We will compare the mAP and precision of the model. The objective of this paper is to identify the model that is best suited for container damage detection. The result is mixed. mAP@50 score of Yolov11 and 12 was 81.9% compared to RF-DETR, which was 77.7%. However, while testing the model for not-so-common damaged containers, the RF-DETR model outperformed the others overall, exhibiting superiority to accurately detecting both damaged containers as well as damage occurrences with high confidence.",\n              "source": "arxiv",\n              "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2506.22517v1",\n              "publication_date": "2025-06-26T14:29:54Z",\n              "journal/conference": "arXiv",\n              "journal_conference": "arXiv",\n              "volume": "",\n              "issue": "",\n              "language": "en",\n              "venue": "arXiv",\n              "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.22517v1",\n              "doi": null,\n              "metadata": {\n                "published": "2025-06-26T14:29:54Z",\n                "arxiv_id": "2506.22517v1",\n                "search_subtopics": [\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "基于视觉的集装箱损伤检测",\n                    "keyword": "(container damage detection and computer vision) or (container surface defect and deep learning)"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱损伤的自动检测系统",\n                    "keyword": "(automated inspection and container damage) or (port container and defect detection system)"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    "subtopic": "集装箱结构损伤与疲劳分析",\n                    "keyword": "(container structural damage and fatigue) or (shipping container and crack detection)"\n                  }\n                ],\n                "found_sources": [\n                  "arxiv"\n                ]\n              }\n            },\n            "note": {\n              "main_question": "比较三种先进计算机视觉模型（Yolov12、Yolov11和RF-DETR）在港口集装箱损伤检测中的性能，以确定最适合该任务的模型。",\n              "methods": [\n                "使用Yolov12、Yolov11和RF-DETR三种计算机视觉模型进行集装箱损伤检测",\n                "使用278张标注图像的数据集进行训练、验证和测试",\n                "比较模型的mAP和精确度指标"\n              ],\n              "datasets": [\n                "278张标注图像的数据集"\n              ],\n              "contributions": [\n                "对三种先进计算机视觉模型在集装箱损伤检测任务上进行了系统比较",\n                "发现Yolov11和Yolov12在mAP@50得分上优于RF-DETR（81.9% vs 77.7%）",\n                "发现RF-DETR在不常见损伤集装箱检测上表现更优，能高置信度准确检测损伤集装箱和损伤发生"\n              ],\n              "limitations": [],\n              "main_results": [\n                "Yolov11和Yolov12的mAP@50得分为81.9%，RF-DETR为77.7%",\n                "RF-DETR在不常见损伤集装箱检测上整体表现优于其他模型"\n              ],\n              "short_summary": "该论文比较了Yolov12、Yolov11和RF-DETR三种模型在港口集装箱损伤检测中的性能，使用278张标注图像的数据集。结果显示Yolov11和Yolov12在mAP@50上优于RF-DETR，但RF-DETR在不常见损伤集装箱检测上表现更优。",\n              "missing_information": [\n                "未提供精确度（precision）的具体数值",\n                "未说明数据集的具体来源和标注方式",\n                "未讨论模型的推理速度或计算资源需求"\n              ],\n              "evidence_level": "abstract"\n            }\n          },\n          "source": "session_artifacts_read"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  "当前草稿": "",\n  "审查整改建议": [],\n  "可用工具": [\n    "get_extraction(List[paperId])：获取论文结构化摘要",\n    "search_section(List[{paperId, List[chunkId]}])：按 chunkId 获取论文原文片段",\n    "get_chunk_by_embed(query)：通过向量检索相关 chunk，当前暂未实现"\n  ]\n}'}], 'model': 'DeepSeek-V4-Flash[free]', 'max_tokens': 5000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.2}} | ctx={"client_host": "127.0.0.1", "method": "POST", "path": "/api/sessions/b28569c2810d4c95a568626d927b3740/runs", "run_id": "run_abc3fcaca9164d70ac2d7c7d70a2f67e", "session_key": "b28569c2810d4c95a568626d927b3740", "turn_id": "834e741a-5514-4b36-8a6c-8f05e80a1c81"}
